Start.
Display the menu: LL, RR, LR, RL, Exit.
Read the user’s choice.
If the choice is Exit, stop. If it is invalid, show an error and go back to step 2.
Select the insertion sequence for the chosen case:
LL: 30, 20, 10
RR: 10, 20, 30
LR: 30, 10, 20
RL: 10, 30, 20
For each key in the sequence, insert it using the standard BST insert, then update the heights of the nodes on the path back to the root.
For each node on that path, compute BF = height(left) − height(right).
If |BF| ≤ 1, the node is balanced. Continue.
If |BF| > 1, identify the case:
BF > 1 and BF(left child) ≥ 0: LL. Display the tree, then apply a right rotation on the node.
BF < −1 and BF(right child) ≤ 0: RR. Display the tree, then apply a left rotation on the node.
BF > 1 and BF(left child) < 0: LR. Display the tree, apply a left rotation on the left child, then a right rotation on the node.
BF < −1 and BF(right child) > 0: RL. Display the tree, apply a right rotation on the right child, then a left rotation on the node.
Display the tree after the rotation, with the balance factor beside each node.
After all keys are inserted, display the final balanced tree.
Return to step 2.
